---
const ledger = [
  {
    n: "01",
    name: "Maps",
    detail: "SharedMap, OR-map, and SharedDirectory: Fluid-derived op semantics, summaries, nested handles, and folder hierarchies",
  },
  {
    n: "02",
    name: "Counters and sets",
    detail: "SharedCounter, G-counter, PN counter, G-set, 2P-set, and OR-set: delta merge, duplicate-safe delivery, add-wins and permanent removal",
  },
  {
    n: "03",
    name: "Sequences and text",
    detail: "SharedSequence and SharedText: grapheme-indexed edits, convergent move, and anchors that survive concurrent edits",
  },
  {
    n: "04",
    name: "Transforms",
    detail: "json_ot and SharedRichText: one client-transform protocol over the ottypes json0 and quill-delta algebras",
  },
  {
    n: "05",
    name: "Coordination",
    detail: "Claims, TaskManager, ordered collection, register collection, and pact map: ownership, work queues with failover, and quorum agreement",
  },
  {
    n: "06",
    name: "Runtime",
    detail: "Server-sequenced delivery, requestOps catch-up, reconnect with client-id remap, nack policy, heartbeat, resubmit, and automatic summaries",
  },
  {
    n: "07",
    name: "App layer",
    detail: "Typed schema decoding, ensure_* bootstrap, presence ripples, Lustre effect bindings, and the in-memory sluice for tests",
  },
];
---

<section class="rigor" aria-labelledby="rigor-title">
  <div class="rigor-inner">
    <div class="guarantees">
      <h2 id="rigor-title">What is implemented and tested</h2>
      <p>
        The runtime is tested three ways: against a reference model, against a
        live floodgate server, and against deliberately nasty orderings of
        operations. The ledger is what those checks cover: everything watershed
        ships.
      </p>
      <dl class="claims">
        <div data-reveal="rise">
          <dt>Property-tested convergence</dt>
          <dd>
            The fuzz harness runs randomized command traces across multiple
            clients, including partial sequencing and delivery, reconnect,
            rollback, stashed ops, and summary-loaded joins. It checks model
            invariants after each command and convergence after a final sync;
            qcheck shrinks failures and the harness records a replayable trace.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div data-reveal="rise">
          <dt>Reference-checked map ops</dt>
          <dd>
            SharedMap’s inner <code>set</code>, <code>delete</code>, and
            <code>clear</code> payloads are checked against a corpus generated
            from <code>@fluidframework/map</code>, including state, events, and
            convergence. Container, attach, and summary formats remain
            watershed’s own.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div data-reveal="rise">
          <dt>Reconnect safety</dt>
          <dd>
            Buffered out-of-order delivery, in-band op requests, and client-id
            remapping on reconnect. Pending edits survive the round trip.
          </dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>

    <div class="ledger-wrap">
      <table class="ledger">
        <caption class="annot">What ships today</caption>
        <tbody>
          {
            ledger.map((row) => (
              <tr data-reveal="rise">
                <th scope="row">{row.n}</th>
                <td>
                  <span class="ledger-name">{row.name}</span>
                  <span class="ledger-detail">{row.detail}</span>
                </td>
              </tr>
            ))
          }
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .rigor {
    padding: var(--space-section) var(--content-pad);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);
  }

  .rigor-inner {
    max-width: 68rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 5fr) minmax(0, 6fr);
    gap: clamp(var(--space-xl), 6vw, 6rem);
    align-items: start;
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: var(--text-h2);
    font-weight: 620;
    font-stretch: 118%;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    line-height: 1.05;
  }

  .guarantees > p {
    margin-top: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .claims {
    margin: var(--space-2xl) 0 0;
  }

  .claims div + div {
    margin-top: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .claims dt {
    font-weight: 650;
    font-stretch: 112%;
    font-size: var(--text-h3);
  }

  .claims dd {
    margin: var(--space-xs) 0 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    max-width: 48ch;
  }

  .claims code {
    font-size: 0.85em;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .ledger-wrap {
    overflow-x: auto;
  }

  .ledger {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    border: 1px solid var(--ink);
  }

  .ledger caption {
    text-align: left;
    padding-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .ledger th,
  .ledger td {
    padding: var(--space-md) var(--space-md);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    vertical-align: baseline;
    text-align: left;
  }

  .ledger tr:first-child th,
  .ledger tr:first-child td {
    border-top: none;
  }

  .ledger th {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--muted);
    width: 3.5rem;
  }

  .ledger-name {
    display: block;
    font-weight: 650;
    font-stretch: 112%;
  }

  .ledger-detail {
    display: block;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-top: var(--space-2xs);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .rigor-inner {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
